; The `syntax/` spellings outside a macro template - reserved, and
; each shape refused where it stands (AX3028). This file is `.axbad`
; because the formatter must not learn these shapes: a name-position
; join outside a template is a formatter REFUSAL, and an arm-position
; syntax/for outside one is silently rewritten into a different tree,
; so committing them as `.ax` would either turn check-fmt red or bake
; mangled bytes.
;
;   line 15/16: a (syntax/join ...) name in ordinary declarations
;   line 18:    a declaration NAMED into the reserved prefix - the
;               one-paren-short near-miss of the join form, which
;               would otherwise silently declare a function called
;               syntax/join taking a and b
;   line 21:    syntax/for in an ordinary match
(:: (syntax/join eq T) (-> Int Int))
(fn ((syntax/join eq T) x) x)

(fn (syntax/join a b) (+ a b))

(:: g Int)
(fn (g) (match 1 (syntax/for (C (syntax/constructors X)) ((C) 1)) (_ 0)))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main) 0)
